{
  "source": "course-assets/wheres-the-line/wheres-the-line.mp4",
  "duration": 201.984,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.44,
      "text": "AI can do remarkable things, but as creators, we the people are responsible for how we use"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.44,
      "end": 6.64,
      "text": "it."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.2,
      "end": 12.28,
      "text": "We exercise this by choosing which tasks to automate and identifying everyone affected"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.28,
      "end": 13.04,
      "text": "by those choices."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.92,
      "end": 14.62,
      "text": "There's a word for this."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.18,
      "end": 15.28,
      "text": "Ethics."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.2,
      "end": 20.7,
      "text": "It means thinking through what you should do and how your decisions affect other people."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.16,
      "end": 25.68,
      "text": "To see how this responsibility plays out in practice, we need to look at a real-world"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.68,
      "end": 29.02,
      "text": "business model where these technical decisions carry serious consequences."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.1,
      "end": 34.64,
      "text": "DraftKings is an online platform where customers play casino games and make sports bets."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.4,
      "end": 37.18,
      "text": "The company earns money when customers lose."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.8,
      "end": 40.22,
      "text": "Traditional casinos operate the exact same way."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.84,
      "end": 43.3,
      "text": "However, some people struggle to control their gambling."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.94,
      "end": 47.34,
      "text": "The challenge is that gambling addiction is a recognized mental health condition,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.8,
      "end": 51.36,
      "text": "one that can seriously impact a person's finances, health, and relationships."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.98,
      "end": 56.08,
      "text": "When customers use DraftKings, they leave a digital record of their betting activity."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.7,
      "end": 62.46,
      "text": "AI can analyze that data to identify specific patterns in how often users play, the size"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.46,
      "end": 64.46,
      "text": "of their bets, and how much money they lose."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.18,
      "end": 66.5,
      "text": "This opens up a thought experiment."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.32,
      "end": 72.58,
      "text": "What if AI could predict which users would gamble and lose more after receiving a special offer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.32,
      "end": 76.74,
      "text": "The system could then trigger an email to those specific users saying,"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.2,
      "end": 79.3,
      "text": "place a bet today and get bonus bets."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.16,
      "end": 81.58,
      "text": "Here is a different thought experiment."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.4,
      "end": 86.5,
      "text": "What if that same AI was used to identify users developing a gambling problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.96,
      "end": 89.64,
      "text": "allowing the company to offer help instead of promotions?"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.88,
      "end": 95.92,
      "text": "When should DraftKings stop encouraging a customer to play if continued gambling could harm them?"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.68,
      "end": 100.42,
      "text": "The New York Times investigated how the company navigated these exact choices,"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.26,
      "end": 101.96,
      "text": "targeted promotions."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.96,
      "end": 107.5,
      "text": "The company developed AI to analyze user habits and premixed which customers would lose"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.5,
      "end": 109.84,
      "text": "more money after receiving free bets and bonuses."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.82,
      "end": 115.02,
      "text": "As for what they did with this system, DraftKings put this technology into active use"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.02,
      "end": 116.46,
      "text": "and continued developing it."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.14,
      "end": 117.92,
      "text": "Customer protection."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.7,
      "end": 122.0,
      "text": "Employees developed a separate AI designed to analyze betting patterns"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.0,
      "end": 125.54,
      "text": "and identify early signs of a gambling problem so the company could intervene."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.3,
      "end": 129.76,
      "text": "In this case, DraftKings chose not to put this predictive technology into use."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.38,
      "end": 133.52,
      "text": "DraftKings disputes the claim that they target users based on losses."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.08,
      "end": 136.4,
      "text": "The company states they already monitor risky behavior"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.4,
      "end": 140.88,
      "text": "and determined there was insufficient evidence that the specific predictive system would be effective."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.7,
      "end": 146.02,
      "text": "AI will do exactly what it is asked to do, even if the end result is harming people."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.8,
      "end": 149.88,
      "text": "Making responsible choices requires four specific moves."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.98,
      "end": 153.72,
      "text": "The first move is to consider everyone affected."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.48,
      "end": 157.22,
      "text": "We have to look beyond the people who benefit from a system"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.22,
      "end": 161.44,
      "text": "and identify who might be harmed, excluded or pressured by it."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.9,
      "end": 164.22,
      "text": "The second move is to be clear with people."
    },
    {
      "start": 164.22,
      "end": 168.92,
      "text": "Explain exactly what the AI system does and how it affects user choices."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.92,
      "end": 171.82,
      "text": "The third move is to build in protection."
    },
    {
      "start": 172.72,
      "end": 178.6,
      "text": "Creators must test for harm, set rigid boundaries and give users a way to challenge AI mistakes."
    },
    {
      "start": 179.4,
      "end": 180.82,
      "text": "Finally, own the outcome."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.72,
      "end": 183.44,
      "text": "Monitor what happens in the real world."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.98,
      "end": 188.84,
      "text": "If the consequences warrant it, you must be willing to change or completely stop the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.4,
      "end": 192.34,
      "text": "A responsible decision considers the people who live with it."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.1,
      "end": 197.3,
      "text": "We the people make the call. What should AI do? That's our responsibility."
    }
  ],
